# Maternal Health Platform — Architecture & Schema (MVP)

Scope note: this covers folder structure and database structure only. No application code. The OCR pipeline itself is out of scope — we assume it hands us a JSON object per uploaded report, and everything below picks up from there.

## Assumptions baked into this design (from your answers)

- **Single doctor / single clinic** for the MVP. No multi-clinic or multi-doctor logic yet — but `clinician_id` is still an explicit foreign key everywhere, so adding a second doctor later is a data change, not a schema change.
- **No separate "pregnancy" entity.** A patient just has appointments. The one thing that genuinely needs a full history across visits is **lab/blood report values** — those get their own timeline table so the clinician dashboard can chart trends.
- **The clinician generates appointment invites** for now (no receptionist role yet). The `profiles.role` field is an enum so a `receptionist` role can be added later without restructuring anything.

